:mp_done_1
There is a knock at the yard door, at one, a plain knock, three times, the same that the Prince's footman uses. It is Ottaviano. He has no hat, and no coach, and his gray coat is wet through, and he says, with great calm, in the doorway, that he has been sent to say that the hand has moved.
It was only for a moment. It made one stroke, and stopped. It was a thing like a letter, a single upright, such as one makes at the beginning of a word. He says that the Prince was in the cellar and saw it. He says that he sat down on the floor.
He says that the Prince does not ask you to come tonight. He says that he thought that you should know.
